# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nexora (ERP RFQ Automation) — repository ignore rules
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# === Secrets / local configuration (NEVER commit) ===
# Real credentials live only here on the dev/demo machine, out of git history.
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.*.Local.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
*.pfx
*.pem
# `.env` itself, not only `.env.local`. deploy/single-box/.env.example instructs the operator to
# `cp .env.example .env` and fill in Jwt__Key, Jwt__PlatformKey, Security__SecretProtectionKey,
# the three CommercialFinance secrets and the database password — and then relies on them
# remembering its "Never commit .env" line, because nothing here covered the bare name. That is
# the single highest-value filename to ignore in this repository and it was the one missing.
# `.env.example` stays tracked via the negation below.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
.env.local
.env.*.local
secrets.json

# === .NET build output ===
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.cache
msbuild.log
project.lock.json
artifacts/

# === Runtime upload content (user data / PII, not source) ===
# These stay on disk (demo still renders them) but must not enter git history.
#
# SEC-G9: the six entries below the marker named paths NOTHING WRITES TO, while the three
# paths the code actually writes were unignored and six demo files were tracked. Verified
# against the writers rather than against the directory listing:
#   ProductRepository.PersistAttachmentAsync  -> wwwroot/ProductAttachments/
#   CustomerController.PersistCustomerImage   -> wwwroot/CustomerImages/
#   UserController                            -> wwwroot/UserImages/   (was already covered)
#   wwwroot/SupplierImages/  — no live writer; tracked content is legacy demo data
# Pre-launch that content is demo data, so nothing here is a live disclosure. It is the
# FIRST pilot tenant to upload a customer logo that puts tenant data in git permanently, and
# git history is the one store this product cannot erase on request.
Backend/ERP_RFQ_Automation/Uploads/
Backend/ERP_RFQ_Automation/wwwroot/CustomerImages/
Backend/ERP_RFQ_Automation/wwwroot/ProductAttachments/
Backend/ERP_RFQ_Automation/wwwroot/SupplierImages/
# The application also creates an Uploads/ tree relative to its WORKING DIRECTORY, which is
# the repository root when it is started from there (Infrastructure/Storage/IFileStorage.cs
# falls back to contentRoot/Uploads). Empty today — git tracks no empty directory — so this
# is the entry that stops the first real ingest from landing in a commit.
/Uploads/
Backend/ERP_RFQ_Automation/wwwroot/uploads/
Backend/ERP_RFQ_Automation/wwwroot/UserImage/
Backend/ERP_RFQ_Automation/wwwroot/UserImages/
Backend/ERP_RFQ_Automation/wwwroot/InventoryImages/
Backend/ERP_RFQ_Automation/wwwroot/ProductImages/

# === Node / Vite frontend ===
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
Frontend/playwright-report*/
Frontend/test-results/

# === OS / editor cruft ===
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# Local E2E run scratch (service logs, generated ids, throwaway credentials)
.e2e-run/
# Logs and scratch from scripts/local/run-platform-console.sh
.local-run/

# Playwright generated output
Frontend/playwright-report/
Frontend/test-results/
